00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:07.055
Service charge is budgeted one block and
one year at a time. This year doesn't have

2
00:00:07.055 --> 00:00:08.555
a budget yet.

3
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:14.101
Start from last year's: the same costs
come across, and so does the month the

4
00:00:14.101 --> 00:00:15.601
year starts.

5
00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:19.705
Add what's new this year — here, a lift
servicing contract — and save.

6
00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:31.638
The total is split by floor area: each
unit's share of the budget, and the

7
00:00:31.638 --> 00:00:33.369
monthly charge that covers it.

8
00:00:34.496 --> 00:00:38.496
Amber means the tenant pays less than
their share today.

9
00:00:41.452 --> 00:00:46.458
Apply to tenants sets everyone's monthly
service charge to match, from their next

10
00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:47.958
invoice.

11
00:00:52.824 --> 00:00:57.997
Budget vs actual tracks what's been spent
against the budget, cost by cost, all

12
00:00:57.997 --> 00:00:59.497
year.

13
00:01:01.863 --> 00:01:06.975
When the year ends, each tenant's share of
what was actually spent is set against

14
00:01:06.975 --> 00:01:08.475
what they were billed.

15
00:01:09.492 --> 00:01:12.992
Days a unit stood empty are the owner's
share.

16
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:20.705
Shortfalls become draft balancing invoices
in one click. Credits are listed for you

17
00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:22.205
to refund.

18
00:01:22.493 --> 00:01:27.335
Publish, and each tenant downloads their
own statement from the portal — or email

19
00:01:27.335 --> 00:01:28.835
it to them.

20
00:01:28.835 --> 00:01:31.508
That's service charge: budget, track,
settle.
